From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Restore Return to Krondor's text bitmap readback.

Return to Krondor draws dynamic UI text into a display-compatible bitmap,
then converts it into an 8-bit sprite using GetDIBits. The game's Rtlib32
does not handle the failed readback, leaving missing text or uninitialized
pixels in the options, credits and book-name screens.

The regression was independently bisected by Bela Gyebroszki to Wine
commit 624a73bcbceec13e57fcfdd8ee2f031f78933395 (fa6a04cda181 in our tree),
which rejects device-dependent bitmaps with depths other than 1 or 32.
His report confirms reverting the commit restores the affected menus.
Local inspection of Rtlib32.dll also shows CreateCompatibleBitmap followed
by DrawTextA and a BI_RGB, 8-bit GetDIBits readback.

Keep the upstream validation for other applications and for format-only
queries, including the SDL3 display-mode query the commit fixes. Allow
only RtK.exe's actual 8-bit BI_RGB readback through the existing conversion
path. Match the executable, not a Steam app ID, to cover GOG installs too.
This is a game-specific compatibility exception, not a general reversion
of the Windows-compatible GetDIBits validation.

Regression diagnosis: Bela Gyebroszki <gyebro69@gmail.com>
GE report: Schweppesale
Wine-Bug: https://bugs.winehq.org/show_bug.cgi?id=60296
GE-Bug: https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/587

Manual validation still required after rebuilding:
- Options: 3D Engine and Next Session names are legible.
- Credits, new-book names and quit confirmation text render correctly.
- Check Software and DirectHAL modes; no D7VK setting should be required.
- Intro playback remains unchanged.

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/dib.c b/dlls/win32u/dib.c
index 09f57676e87..f611489bd06 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/dib.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/dib.c
@@ -1195,6 +1195,17 @@ BITMAPINFO *copy_packed_dib( const BITMAPINFO *src_info, UINT usage )
     return ret;
 }
 
+static BOOL use_krondor_bitmap_readback(void)
+{
+    static const WCHAR rtkW[] = {'R','t','K','.','e','x','e',0};
+    const WCHAR *p, *name = NtCurrentTeb()->Peb->ProcessParameters->ImagePathName.Buffer;
+
+    if (!name) return FALSE;
+    if ((p = wcsrchr( name, '/' ))) name = p + 1;
+    if ((p = wcsrchr( name, '\\' ))) name = p + 1;
+    return !wcsicmp( name, rtkW );
+}
+
 /******************************************************************************
  *           NtGdiGetDIBitsInternal    (win32u.@)
  *
@@ -1349,7 +1360,11 @@ INT WINAPI NtGdiGetDIBitsInternal( HDC hdc, HBITMAP hbitmap, UINT startscan, UIN
 
     if (err) goto done;
 
-    if (!is_bitmapobj_dib( bmp ) && (src_info->bmiHeader.biBitCount != 1 && src_info->bmiHeader.biBitCount != 32))
+    /* RtK converts text drawn into display-depth DDBs to 8-bit sprites. Keep
+     * format-only queries unchanged, including SDL3's display-mode probe. */
+    if (!is_bitmapobj_dib( bmp ) && (src_info->bmiHeader.biBitCount != 1 && src_info->bmiHeader.biBitCount != 32)
+            && !(bits && dst_info->bmiHeader.biBitCount == 8 && dst_info->bmiHeader.biCompression == BI_RGB
+                 && use_krondor_bitmap_readback()))
         goto done;
 
     /* fill out the src colour table, if it needs one */
